+# Send pickup reminders by SMS
+
+For whoever proposes email reminders to save the SMS cost, or changes `larder/reminders.py`. The day-before pickup
+reminder goes by SMS, about 40 euros a month, because missed pickups doubled during a trial of email reminders.
+
+## Context
+
+From April to June 2025 pickup reminders went by email to save the SMS cost. The email provider's report showed 34% of
+the reminder emails were never opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% of pantry orders to 13%. Each missed pickup is a
+packed bag whose fresh food goes in the bin by closing time. Many members share one phone in the family and never
+check email; an SMS they see. Reminders went back to SMS on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August.
+Email was proposed again in [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md) in September, the third time that year. Two forces
+judge the options: a member must see the reminder, or the bag and its fresh food are wasted; and the pantry runs on
+little money, so a recurring cost needs a reason.
+
+## Options
+
+- **Email**: free, and every member has an address on file; lost on the first force, as the 2025 trial showed: a third
+  of the emails went unopened and missed pickups doubled.
+- **SMS**: about 40 euros a month; chosen.
+
+## Decision
+
+Pickup reminders go by SMS, because members see an SMS and missed pickups stay at 6%; the food a doubled rate of missed
+pickups throws away is worth more to the pantry than 40 euros a month.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Members see their reminders and fewer bags are wasted. The pantry pays about 40 euros a month for SMS. The email path
+stays in `larder/reminders.py`, behind `CHANNEL`, so switching is one line; a new proposal should bring evidence that
+members would now open the emails, such as a trial measuring missed pickups.
